---
title: "handle_withdraw (Pebble Protocol: Market Internal)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_amount: assert ctoken_amount != 0
    q_check_amount --> q_load_asset: asset = assets.load_by_type(name)
    q_load_asset --> q_check_paused: assert !withdraw_paused
    q_check_paused --> q_load_obligation: obligation = obligations.borrow_mut(obligation_id)
    q_load_obligation --> q_check_market: assert obligation.market_id() == self.id
    q_check_market --> q_refresh_all: refresh_obligation_assets_interest(all debts + collaterals)
    q_refresh_all --> q_withdraw_ctokens: ctoken = obligation.withdraw_ctokens(ctoken_amount)
    q_withdraw_ctokens --> q_safety_check: is_obligation_safe(oracle, registry, clock)
    q_safety_check --> q_error_unsafe: not safe
    q_error_unsafe --> [*]: abort obligation_not_safe
    q_safety_check --> q_burn: deposit = reserve.burn_ctokens(ctoken)
    q_burn --> q_rate_limit: emode.deposit_limiter.add_outflow(now, deposit.value())
    q_rate_limit --> q_try_stop_adl: try_stop_collateral_deleverage if applicable
    q_try_stop_adl --> [*]: return (deposit_coin, ctokens_left)

    note right of q_withdraw_ctokens
        INV-001: obligation must support this collateral token
        INV-002: ctoken balance must be sufficient
    end note

    note right of q_burn
        INV-003: redeem_amount = exchange_rate * ctoken_amount
        INV-004: cash must remain >= cash_reserve after withdrawal
        INV-005: total_supply decreases by burned ctoken amount
    end note
